cle boundaries. For example, an RPG quest links narrative and save state; an IDE edit links language analysis, workspace indexing, and version control; an OS permission links identity, process, storage, and user settings.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"02-feature-model.md Domain relationship map and invariants records cross-domain content, round, save, update, and deletion boundaries.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Every game has a game-design bible that selects only relevant genre modules, maps stable `GAME-*` units to first-release journeys and implementation domains, and gives each selected module a bounded content/production plan.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"02-game-design-bible.md/.json define three relevant modules, GAME-001\u2013012, implementation_map, and bounded production plans; repaired manifest accepts each module.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The game-bible JSON has non-empty `game_archetypes`, `selected_modules`, and `design_units`; every selected module owns at least one `GAME-*` design unit and every unit records its module, player outcome, production mode, and first-release scope. Rejected modules record why they are not part of this game, rather than being silently omitted.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"02-game-design-bible.json has non-empty required arrays, explicit rejected modules, and complete GAME-001\u2013012 fields; validator passes selected-module and inventory checks.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Finite content is represented by concrete original design cards; scalable content is represented by a catalogue rule, quantity/distribution, source or provenance policy, and bounded production batches. This applies equally to RPG content, trivia questions, puzzle packs, races, strategy units, and any other game-specific content.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"GAME-002 defines 48 original Kickoff Mix cards in four 12-card reviewed batches; GAME-005 defines TUT-01\u2013TUT-05; GAME-004 defines the scalable editorial/anti-repeat rule.\"},{\"criterio